Track 1: Blown Cylinders Swallow the Gale
- Story & Context: On the night Hurricane Cleo sheared the roof off the Morant Bay broadcast shed, Sister Orla jammed a broken lead-crystal glass pipe into the transmitter's blown cooling vent to keep the signal live while seawater swirled around her ankles. The ribbon microphone caught the sound of rain clattering like gravel against zinc, her baritone horn droning two desolate, unyielding notes that rode the thunderclap all the way to receivers thirty miles inland. Fishermen pulled their skiffs ashore just to listen to the dying broadcast shudder across the 108.4 band, capturing the exact second the frequency died on tape. Her voice emerged through the brine like a siren across the reefs: "The glass will melt before this horn gives back the sky."
